[FINAL-TEXT] === DIAGNOSIS ===
is_anomaly: true
faulty_devices: router1
diagnosis_text:
Affected component: the inter-router link on router1 (interface eth0) is administratively down, preventing the BGP session and transit routing between AS1 and AS2.

Mechanism: With router1:eth0 down, router1 has no connected route to the interconnect 193.10.11.0/24 and cannot reach its BGP neighbor (193.10.11.2). As a result, BGP on router1 remains in Active and never establishes, so router1 does not learn 200.1.1.0/24. When pc1 (195.11.14.2) tries to reach pc2 (200.1.1.2), router1 immediately returns ICMP “Destination Net Unreachable.”

Localization and evidence:
- router1 ip/ifconfig shows eth0 state DOWN and no 193.10.11.0/24 route; only 195.11.14.0/24 is present.
- Ping router1->router2 fails: “Network is unreachable.”
- BGP on router1: neighbor 193.10.11.2 is in Active with 0 prefixes received.
- pc1->pc2 ping returns “From 195.11.14.1 Destination Net Unreachable,” proving the block is at router1.
- FRR is running on both routers, and BGP configs are correct (neighbors and network statements present), so no rollback is needed.

Root cause: router1’s inter-AS interface (eth0) was left administratively down.

Corrective fix: Bring router1:eth0 up (ip link set dev eth0 up). BGP will re-establish automatically and routes will be exchanged. If a restart is preferred by operations, restart the router1 device (or its networking service); do not change BGP configuration.
=== END ===